# Byte fidelity for the publish gate.
#
# The S6 gate hashes the EXACT dist bytes, commits them, and then re-hashes what
# GitHub Pages actually serves. Any line-ending normalisation between those two
# points silently changes the hash of every text asset, so the live byte-identity
# check would fail on files that are in fact correct - or worse, pass locally and
# ship subtly different bytes.
#
# `* -text` disables ALL text conversion: git stores and checks out exactly the
# bytes it was given. Combined with `core.autocrlf false` this makes the hash
# recorded in docs/publish/PUBLISH.md meaningful.
* -text
